    "name": "common-alder",
    "notes": "THE ROOTS ARE THE POINT AND THEY ARE REAL GEOMETRY. `roots.count` 7 with a long reach and a high arch draws ridges humping out of the base and back down to the ground, which is what an alder standing in water looks like. That is distinct from `trunk.buttress`, which only thickens the cylinder -- the alder uses both.\n\nPlaced hard against water: `water_max_m` 8 and a very low slope ceiling, so it lines channels rather than filling woods. Dark, narrow, and irregular.",
